<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40645" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕ-corrĭgo</span></b> , rexi,
			rectum, 3, v. a.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>to mend</i> or <i>correct again</i> (post-Aug. and very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">costas,</span>”
				i. e. <i>to set right again</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 43, 4</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to amend</i>, <i>reform</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 50, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquem ad regulam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 4, 5</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
